r or .divider), CSS-only grain/noise overlay: a fixed full-viewport pseudo-element (body::after) using an inline SVG feTurbulence noise as data-URI background, opacity ~0.05, pointer-events:none, mix-blend-mode:overlay.\\nGlass-like dark panels: background var(--panel), backdrop-filter:blur(10px), 1px solid var(--border), border-radius ~16px.\\nButtons: .btn (gold fill variant: background linear-gradient gold→soft gold, dark text; ghost variant: transparent with gold border, ivory text). Visible hover (lift translateY(-2px), glow box-shadow) and :focus-visible outline in gold. border-radius 999px pill buttons.\\nScroll reveal: elements with .reveal start opacity:0, translateY(28px); .reveal.visible transitions to visible (transition ~0.8s cubic-bezier). Respect prefers-reduced-motion.\\nSmooth scrolling: html{scroll-behavior:smooth} plus scroll-padding-top for sticky nav offset.\\nStrong typographic hierarchy: section eyebrow labels (small uppercase letter-spaced gold sans), big serif section titles, thin gold divider under titles.\\n\\n=== SECTIONS (single page, sticky navbar, smooth scroll) ===\\n\\n1) NAVBAR (sticky, top:0, z-index high, background rgba(7,5,6,0.75) + backdrop blur + bottom 1px var(--border)):\\n- Logo \\\"ARTIFACT\\\" — serif, ivory, gold diamond ◆ accent before it.\\n- Links: Program, Artists, Venue, Tickets, FAQ (anchor links to section ids #program #artists #venue #tickets #faq).\\n- CTA button \\\"Get Tickets\\\" (gold, links to #tickets).\\n- Active nav state while scrolling: JS scroll-spy highlights the current section's link (gold color + small underline).\\n- Mobile: hamburger button (3 lines, aria-expanded, aria-controls) toggling a full-width dropdown panel under the navbar; links close the menu on click. Responsive below ~860px.\\n\\n2) HERO (id=\\\"top\\\", full viewport min-height:100vh, cinematic editorial layout):\\n- Background image https://source.unsplash.com/featured/2400x1400?museum,night with dark overlay (linear-gradient from rgba(7,5,6,0.92) through rgba(7,5,6,0.55)) plus a spotlight radial-gradient (soft gold, top center) and vignette. Use a <div class=\\\"hero-bg\\\"> with background-image or an <img> absolutely positioned + overlay divs.\\n- Eyebrow: \\\"ARTIFACT: Museum Night\\\" (small gold uppercase).\\n- Huge serif headline: \\\"Museum Night, Reimagined\\\" (clamp font-size ~3rem–6.5rem, italic accent word optional).\\n- Sub copy line: one elegant sentence about the night.\\n- Metadata badges row (small glass pills with gold border): \\\"18 October 2026\\\", \\\"19:00–02:00\\\", \\\"The Old Gallery, Warsaw\\\".\\n- CTA row: \\\"Get Tickets\\\" (gold, href #tickets) and \\\"Save to Calendar\\\" (ghost button, id for JS .ics download).\\n- Scroll hint at bottom (small \\\"Scroll\\\" + animated line/chevron).\\n\\n3) CONCEPT / INTRO (id=\\\"concept\\\"):\\n- Editorial paragraph (2–3 sentences, serif lead-in) about one night when the museum stays awake — velvet darkness, golden spotlights, quiet mystery.\\n- 3 feature cards (glass panels, hover lift + gold border glow): \\\"After-hours exhibitions\\\", \\\"Live performances\\\", \\\"Guided hidden-room tours\\\" — each with a small inline SVG icon (gold stroke), title, 1–2 sentence description.\\n\\n4) PROGRAM TIMELINE (id=\\\"program\\\"):\\n- Vertical timeline, center or left gold line with dots. Items (time, title, short description, location tag pill):\\n  19:00 — Doors Open — \\\"Champagne welcome in the candlelit foyer.\\\" — Grand Foyer\\n  19:30 — Curator Welcome — \\\"Chief curator opens the night with a short address.\\\" — Main Hall\\n  20:00 — Hidden Collection Tour — \\\"Rarely shown works from the vaults, in small groups.\\\" — Vault Rooms\\n  21:00 — Live Ambient Performance — \\\"Modular soundscape among the masters.\\\" — East Wing\\n  22:00 — Sculpture Hall Projection — \\\"Light and shadow mapped across marble.\\\" — Sculpture Hall\\n  23:00 — Artist Talk — \\\"Conversation with this year's featured artists.\\\" —