      "metadata": "{\"path\":\"website_museum_openrouter-moonshotai-kimi-k3_01.html\",\"mode\":\"llm_assisted\",\"diff_lines\":1382,\"added_lines\":1377,\"removed_lines\":0,\"noop\":false,\"edit_description\":\"Create a NEW complete single-file HTML website (the file does not exist yet — generate the entire file from scratch). It is a premium cinematic event landing page for \\\"ARTIFACT: Museum Night\\\". STRICT: one HTML file only, HTML + inline CSS (one <style> block in <head>) + inline vanilla JavaScript (one <script> block before </body>). NO frameworks, NO libraries, NO external CSS/JS. Remote images allowed. Must work when opened directly from disk (file://).\\n\\n=== SEO / META (in <head>) ===\\n- <title>ARTIFACT: Museum Night — Museum Night, Reimagined</title>\\n- meta description: \\\"ARTIFACT: Museum Night — a cinematic after-hours museum event at The Old Gallery, Warsaw. 18 October 2026, 19:00–02:00. Exhibitions, live performances, talks and hidden-room tours.\\\"\\n- Open Graph tags: og:title, og:description, og:image (use https://source.unsplash.com/featured/2400x1400?museum,night), og:type=website\\n- Inline SVG favicon via data URI: a small gold (#d6ad60) diamond/monogram \\\"A\\\" on dark background, e.g. <link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:image/svg+xml,...\\\"> (URL-encode the SVG properly).\\n\\n=== DESIGN SYSTEM (CSS custom properties on :root) ===\\nColors: --bg:#070506; --velvet:#1a0710; --burgundy:#3a0f1d; --navy:#07111f; --gold:#d6ad60; --gold-soft:#f3d79b; --ivory:#f8efe2; --muted:#b9a999; --panel:rgba(255,244,220,0.06); --border:rgba(214,173,96,0.28).\\nTypography: headlines font-family: Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif (elegant, large, tight letter-spacing, ivory with gold accents); body font-family: Inter,system-ui,'Segoe UI',sans-serif; muted text color for secondary copy.\\nGlobal look: near-black velvet background with layered radial/conic gradients (burgundy glow top-left, midnight navy glow bottom-right), soft spotlight effects (large radial-gradient overlays with gold at low opacity), thin gold divider lines (1px gradient hr or .divider), CSS-only grain/noise overlay: a fixed full-viewport pseudo-element (body::after) using an inline SVG feTurbulence noise as data-URI background, opacity ~0.05, pointer-events:none, mix-blend-mode:overlay.\\nGlass-like dark panels: background var(--panel), backdrop-filter:blur(10px), 1px solid var(--border), border-radius ~16px.\\nButtons: .btn (gold fill variant: background linear-gradient gold→soft gold, dark text; ghost variant: transparent with gold border, ivory text). Visible hover (lift translateY(-2px), glow box-shadow) and :focus-visible outline in gold. border-radius 999px pill buttons.\\nScroll reveal: elements with .reveal start opacity:0, translateY(28px); .reveal.visible transitions to visible (transition ~0.8s cubic-bezier). Respect prefers-reduced-motion.\\nSmooth scrolling: html{scroll-behavior:smooth} plus scroll-padding-top for sticky nav offset.\\nStrong typographic hierarchy: section eyebrow labels (small uppercase letter-spaced gold sans), big serif section titles, thin gold divider under titles.\\n\\n=== SECTIONS (single page, sticky navbar, smooth scroll) ===\\n\\n1) NAVBAR (sticky, top:0, z-index high, background rgba(7,5,6,0.75) + backdrop blur + bottom 1px var(--border)):\\n- Logo \\\"ARTIFACT\\\" — serif, ivory, gold diamond ◆ accent before it.\\n- Links: Program, Artists, Venue, Tickets, FAQ (anchor links to section ids #program #artists #venue #tickets #faq).\\n- CTA button \\\"Get Tickets\\\" (gold, links to #tickets).\\n- Active nav state while scrolling: JS scroll-spy highlights the current section's link (gold color + small underline).\\n- Mobile: hamburger button (3 lines, aria-expanded, aria-controls) toggling a full-width dropdown panel under the navbar; links close the menu on click. Responsive below ~860px.\\n\\n2) HERO (id=\\\"top\\\", full viewport min-height:100vh, cinematic editorial layout):\\n- Background image https://source.unsplash.com/featured/2400x1400?museum,night with dark overlay (linear-gradient from rgba(7,5,6,0.92) through rgba(7,5,6,0.55)) plus a spotlight radial-gradient (soft gold, top center) and vignette. Use a <div class=\\\"hero-bg\\\"> with background-image or an <img> absolutely positioned + overlay divs.\\n- Eyebrow: \\\"ARTIFACT: Museum Night\\\" (small gold uppercase).\\n- Huge serif headline: \\\"Museum Night, Reimagined\\\" (clamp font-size ~3rem–6.5rem, italic accent word optional).\\n- Sub copy line: one elegant sentence about the night.\\n- Metadata badges row (small glass pills with gold border): \\\"18 October 2026\\\", \\\"19:00–02:00\\\", \\\"The Old Gallery, Warsaw\\\".\\n- CTA row: \\\"Get Tickets\\\" (gold, href #tickets) and \\\"Save to Calendar\\\" (ghost button, id for JS .ics download).\\n- Scroll hint at bottom (small \\\"Scroll\\\" + animated line/chevron).\\n\\n3) CONCEPT / INTRO (id=\\\"concept\\\"):\\n- Editorial paragraph (2–3 sentences, serif lead-in) about one night when the museum stays awake — velvet darkness, golden spotlights, quiet mystery.\\n- 3 feature cards (glass panels, hover lift + gold border glow): \\\"After-hours exhibitions\\\", \\\"Live performances\\\", \\\"Guided hidden-room tours\\\" — each with a small inline SVG icon (gold stroke), title, 1–2 sentence description.\\n\\n4) PROGRAM TIMELINE (id=\\\"program\\\"):\\n- Vertical timeline, center or left gold line with dots. Items (time, title, short description, location tag pill):\\n  19:00 — Doors Open — \\\"Champagne welcome in the candlelit foyer.\\\" — Grand Foyer\\n  19:30 — Curator Welcome — \\\"Chief curator opens the night with a short address.\\\" — Main Hall\\n  20:00 — Hidden Collection Tour — \\\"Rarely shown works from the vaults, in small groups.\\\" — Vault Rooms\\n  21:00 — Live Ambient Performance — \\\"Modular soundscape among the masters.\\\" — East Wing\\n  22:00 — Sculpture Hall Projection — \\\"Light and shadow mapped across marble.\\\" — Sculpture Hall\\n  23:00 — Artist Talk — \\\"Conversation with this year's featured artists.\\\" — Auditorium\\n  00:00 — Midnight Gallery Walk — \\\"A slow, silent walk through the darkened galleries.\\\" — All Galleries\\n  01:00 — Closing Sound Session — \\\"A final ambient set as the night dissolves.\\\" — Courtyard\\n- Alternate items left/right on desktop (asymmetric), stacked on mobile. Reveal animations.\\n\\n5) ARTISTS / SPEAKERS (id=\\\"artists\\\"):\\n- 8 cards in a responsive grid (asymmetric: some cards span/taller on desktop). Each card: image (top), name (serif), role (gold small caps), 1-line teaser, \\\"View details\\\" button (ghost, small).\\n- Images (in order, reuse last two for cards 7–8):\\n  1 https://source.unsplash.com/featured/1200x900?gallery,art\\n  2 https://source.unsplash.com/featured/1200x900?exhibition,lights\\n  3 https://source.unsplash.com/featured/1200x900?sculpture,museum\\n  4 https://source.unsplash.com/featured/1200x900?museum,crowd\\n  5 https://source.unsplash.com/featured/1200x900?art,installation\\n  6 https://source.unsplash.com/featured/1200x900?theater,stage\\n  (cards 7 and 8 reuse images 1 and 3)\\n- Artists (name / role / teaser / session time):\\n  1. Elena Voss — Light Installation Artist — \\\"Paints with beams across baroque ceilings.\\\" — 21:00, East Wing\\n  2. Marcus Hale — Ambient Composer — \\\"Modular synths in dialogue with old masters.\\\" — 21:00, East Wing\\n  3. Dr. Ingrid Sauer — Chief Curator — \\\"Keeper of the vaults and their quiet secrets.\\\" — 19:30, Main Hall\\n  4. Tomasz Nowak — Projection Artist — \\\"Turns marble into moving cinema.\\\" — 22:00, Sculpture Hall\\n  5. Amara Diallo — Performance Artist — \\\"Slow movement studies in the darkened halls.\\\" — 00:00, All Galleries\\n  6. Viktor Lindqvist — Sound Designer — \\\"Closes the night with a dissolving soundscape.\\\" — 01:00, Courtyard\\n  7. Sofia Marchetti — Art Historian — \\\"Stories the guidebooks never printed.\\\" — 20:00, Vault Rooms\\n  8. Jan Kowalczyk — Photographer — \\\"Documenting the museum after dark.\\\" — 23:00, Auditorium\\n- ARTIST MODAL: accessible modal (role=\\\"dialog\\\", aria-modal=\\\"true\\\", aria-labelledby). Opens on \\\"View details\\\" with that artist's name, role, image, longer bio (write a 2–3 sentence bio per artist in JS data), session time, and a close button (×). Close on ESC, close on backdrop click, return focus to the triggering button, basic focus trap (keep Tab within modal). Body scroll locked while open.\\n\\n6) VENUE (id=\\\"venue\\\"):\\n- Two-column layout: left = venue info; right = inline SVG map mock.\\n- Info: venue name \\\"The Old Gallery\\\", address \\\"ul. Królewska 12, 00-001 Warsaw\\\", travel tips (arrive 15 min early; cloakroom at the entrance; last entry 23:30), accessibility notes (step-free entrance, lifts to all floors, quiet room available), parking / public transport notes (metro M2 Świętokrzyska, buses 175/128, paid parking behind the gallery).\\n- Inline SVG map mock (dark panel background): a gold-outlined rectangle \\\"The Old Gallery\\\" block, nearby street lines (thin muted strokes with small street labels), a metro marker (circle \\\"M\\\") and bus marker (\\\"B\\\"), an entrance marker (gold dot + \\\"Entrance\\\" label), and a dashed gold route line from metro to entrance. Include subtle grid/labels; keep it elegant, gold/ivory on dark.\\n\\n7) TICKET TIERS (id=\\\"tickets\\\"):\\n- 3 premium ticket cards (glass panels, hover highlight: lift + gold border + glow). Middle card featured (slightly larger, \\\"Recommended\\\" badge in gold).\\n- Tier 1 \\\"Night Pass\\\" €29: Entry after 19:00; Main exhibition access; Program access.\\n- Tier 2 \\\"Curator Pass\\\" €59 (Recommended): Everything in Night Pass; Hidden collection tour; Reserved artist talk seating.\\n- Tier 3 \\\"Patron Pass\\\" €129: Everything in Curator Pass; VIP lounge access; Signed event print; Priority entrance.\\n- Each card: feature list with gold ✓ marks, price large serif, \\\"Select\\\" button.\\n- TICKET CHECKOUT MODAL (accessible like artist modal): shows selected tier name + unit price; fields: attendee name (text), email (email), number of tickets (select 1–6 or number input min 1 max 6); live total price (qty × price, formatted €); checkbox \\\"I accept the terms of the event\\\"; \\\"Confirm reservation\\\" button. Validation: name required (min 2 chars), valid email regex, qty 1–6, terms must be checked — inline error messages under fields (red-ish/gold), aria-invalid. On success: close modal + show success toast \\\"Reservation confirmed — Night Pass ×2 · €58\\\" (or keep modal open showing a success state with checkmark; either fine). NO real payment — note in modal: \\\"Demo checkout — no payment is processed.\\\"\\n\\n8) FAQ ACCORDION (id=\\\"faq\\\") — at least these 6 (button + panel, aria-expanded, smooth max-height/transition, only one open at a time, chevron rotates):\\n- Is payment processed on this page? — No. This is a demo landing page; reservations are mock and no payment is collected.\\n- Can I arrive late? — Yes, last entry is 23:30; some tours have fixed start times.\\n- Are photos allowed? — Yes, without flash; tripods and professional rigs are not permitted.\\n- Is the venue accessible? — Step-free entrance, lifts to all floors, accessible restrooms, quiet room.\\n- Can I change my ticket tier? — Yes, up to 7 days before the event via your confirmation email link.\\n- How do I save the event to my calendar? — Use the \\\"Save to Calendar\\\" button at the top; it downloads an .ics file.\\n\\n9) NEWSLETTER (id=\\\"newsletter\\\"): glass panel with serif title \\\"Letters from the museum\\\", email input + \\\"Subscribe\\\" button. Inline validation (valid email regex, error message under field), on success show toast \\\"You're on the list — see you in the dark.\\\" and clear input.\\n\\n10) FOOTER: ARTIFACT logo, event credits line (\\\"Curated by the Old Gallery team · Visual identity: Studio Artifact\\\"), social-style text links (Instagram, Facebook, YouTube — href=\\\"#\\\" with aria-labels), copyright \\\"© 2026 ARTIFACT: Museum Night\\\", and small muted note: \\\"Demo landing page — no real ticket purchase.\\\"\\n\\n=== SPECIAL FEATURE — SAVE TO CALENDAR (.ics) ===\\nJS function on the \\\"Save to Calendar\\\" button(s): build an ICS string with BEGIN:VCALENDAR / VERSION:2.0 / PRODID / BEGIN:VEVENT / UID (unique-ish) / DTSTAMP / DTSTART:20261018T190000 / DTEND:20261019T020000 / SUMMARY:ARTIFACT: Museum Night / LOCATION:The Old Gallery, Warsaw / DESCRIPTION:A cinematic after-hours museum event with exhibitions, performances, talks, and guided tours. / END:VEVENT / END:VCALENDAR (CRLF line endings). Create a Blob (type text/calendar), URL.createObjectURL, temporary <a download=\\\"artifact-museum-night.ics\\\">, click it, revoke URL. Show toast \\\"Calendar file downloaded.\\\" Works fully client-side.\\n\\n=== TOASTS ===\\nFixed bottom-right toast container; JS showToast(message) creates a dark glass toast with gold left border, slides/fades in, auto-removes after ~3.5s. role=\\\"status\\\" aria-live=\\\"polite\\\".\\n\\n=== JAVASCRIPT (vanilla, no console errors) ===\\n- Scroll-spy: IntersectionObserver on sections toggling .active on matching nav links.\\n- Reveal: IntersectionObserver adding .visible to .reveal elements (unobserve after).\\n- Mobile menu toggle.\\n- Artist data array (8 artists with bio) + modal open/close with focus management (ESC, backdrop, focus trap, restore focus).\\n- Ticket modal: open with tier data (name, price), live total computation, validation, success toast.\\n- FAQ accordion.\\n- Newsletter validation + toast.\\n- Save-to-calendar .ics generation.\\n- Footer year auto (optional).\\n- All JS wrapped in IIFE / DOMContentLoaded; guard nulls; no console errors.\\n\\n=== RESPONSIVE ===\\nMobile-first-ish breakpoints ~960px and ~640px: nav collapses to hamburger, hero headline scales with clamp, timeline stacks, artist grid 1–2 columns, ticket cards stack, venue stacks, modal padding adjusts.\\n\\n=== QUALITY BAR ===\\nProduction-ready, polished, cohesive cinematic look: velvet darkness, golden spotlights, quiet mystery. Smooth hover states everywhere, thin gold dividers between sections, generous whitespace. No console errors. All ids referenced by JS must exist. Escape & in text as &amp; where needed. Write the COMPLETE file.\",\"model\":\"moonshotai/kimi-k3\",\"provider\":\"openrouter\",\"tokens_in\":4594,\"tokens_out\":21209,\"cost_usd\":0.0557789,\"tool_name\":\"advance_code_editing\"}",
